  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "JavaScript EPSILON"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Number.EPSILON is the difference between\nthe smallest floating point number greater than 1 and 1."
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "let x = Number.EPSILON;",
   "caption": "Example"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_number_epsilon"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Number.EPSILON is an ES6 feature."
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "It does not work in Internet Explorer."
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "JavaScript MAX_VALUE"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Number.MAX_VALUE is a constant representing the largest possible number in JavaScript."
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "let x = Number.MAX_VALUE;",
   "caption": "Example"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_number_max"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "Number Properties Cannot be Used on Variables"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Number properties belong to the JavaScript Number Object."
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "These properties can only be accessed as Number.MAX_VALUE."
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Using x.MAX_VALUE, where x is a variable or a value,\nwill return undefined:"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "let x = 6;\n\nx.MAX_VALUE",
   "caption": "Example"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_number_max_undefined"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "JavaScript MIN_VALUE"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Number.MIN_VALUE is a constant representing the lowest possible number in JavaScript."
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "let x = Number.MIN_VALUE;",
   "caption": "Example"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_number_min"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "Minimum and Maximum Safe Integers"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "ES6 added max and min properties to the Number object:"
  },
  {
   "type": "list",
   "ordered": false,
   "items": [
    "Number.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER",
    "Number.MIN_SAFE_INTEGER"
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "JavaScript MIN_SAFE_INTEGER"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Number.MIN_SAFE_INTEGER represents the minimum safe integer in JavaScript."
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Number.MIN_SAFE_INTEGER is -(253 - 1)."
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "let x = Number.MIN_SAFE_INTEGER;",
   "caption": "Example"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_number_min_safe"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "JavaScript MAX_SAFE_INTEGER"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Number.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER represents the maximum safe integer in JavaScript."
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Number.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER is (253 - 1)."
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "let x = Number.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER;",
   "caption": "Example"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_number_max_safe"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "JavaScript POSITIVE_INFINITY"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "let x = Number.POSITIVE_INFINITY;",
   "caption": "Example"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "let x = 1 / 0;",
   "caption": "Example"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_number_pos_infinity"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "JavaScript NEGATIVE_INFINITY"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "let x = Number.NEGATIVE_INFINITY;",
   "caption": "Example"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "let x = -1 / 0;",
   "caption": "Example"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_number_neg_infinity"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "JavaScript NaN - Not a Number"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "NaN is a JavaScript reserved word for a number that is not a legal number."
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "let x = Number.NaN;",
   "caption": "Examples"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "let x = 100 / \"Apple\";",
   "caption": "Examples"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_number_nan"
  },
